# Normalise every text file to LF, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows rewrites CRLF on checkout while
# files written by editors stay LF, so one tree ends up mixed — `content/utils/
# _index.md` was literally half CRLF and half LF. `build.rs` used to defend
# against that with an explicit `\r\n` pass in `split_frontmatter`; the real fix
# belongs here, at the source. `eol=lf` overrides `core.autocrlf` on checkout,
# so the working tree stays consistent whichever machine clones it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary media must never be line-ending converted or diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.svg text
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary

# The lockfile is generated and must stay byte-exact.
Cargo.lock text eol=lf
